{
  "name": "JsonIsItemsKind",
  "comment": "A json value is item's, not text's (ruling 2, decisions 773 + 774 + 787). A json value\ncan hold any value (a number, a bool, a list, a dict), so its parent is item, not text:\nType={item, kind: json} lands as an item whose kind navigates as the \"json\" type. The\nasserts are ordered by state: first, while %x% is unread, type.name is \"item\" and the\nkind navigates as \"json\"; then `%x% is text` reads x — the parsed json is a plang dict\n— so after the read %x% is text is false and type.name narrows to \"dict\". A value's\ntype is what it is now, and its history is where it came from (787).",
  "step": [
